                </p>
                <h3 style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 20px;">Economic Development – City of Cheyenne.</h3>
                <p style="font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.6;">
                    In 2006, the citizens of Cheyenne, Wyoming, finalized a new comprehensive plan for their community. PlanCheyenne won the American Planning Association and garnered national attention for its innovative approach to community planning by integrating parks and land-use planning, urban character, and community design in a joint city/county planning effort. In the years following implementation, the plan helped the city generate significant growth in the technology sector, including the establishment of a major data center by the Microsoft Corporation, as well as other data centers.
                </p>
                <p style="font-size: 11pt; line-height: 1.6;">
                    In 2014, the City of Cheyenne revisited and updated its plan with PlanCheyenne: Reflections and Progress.
                </p>
